# Calculators and the spreadsheets, one stanza per program.

shot    loan
size    30 80
cap     An amortisation calculator.  Principal, term in years, rate and
cap     the starting month go in, and out comes the payment, the total
cap     interest and a month-by-month schedule with a subtotal at each
cap     year.  Fed from a file here, because it asks its questions on one
cap     line; 120,000 over thirty years at 6.5% is 758.48 a month.
run     mkdir -p /dd/tmp/MTH > /nil 2>/nil; printf "120000\r30\r6.5\r8\rs\r" > /dd/tmp/MTH/la
wait    2
run     clear
wait    1
run     loan < /dd/tmp/MTH/la | head -n 22
wait    10

shot    cvtbase
cap     Converts a number between bases.  The bases are named by key --
cap     d for decimal, h or x for hex, b for binary, o for octal -- and
cap     the number arrives on standard input.
run     echo 255 | cvtbase d h
wait    4
run     echo 255 | cvtbase d b
wait    4
run     echo ff | cvtbase h d
wait    4

shot    rechne
cap     A German command-line calculator: every answer in decimal, hex
cap     and binary at once.  The expression is one argument with no
cap     spaces in it; x multiplies and m is modulo.
run     rechne 4095+1
wait    2
run     rechne 12x12
wait    2
run     rechne \$ff+1
wait    2
run     rechne 100m7
wait    2
run     rechne -b 12345
wait    3

shot    rpn
cap     A reverse-Polish calculator, and this is it going wrong: 12 and
cap     34 push correctly, and then + pushes a 0 on top of them instead of
cap     replacing them with 46.  rechne is the calculator that answers.
run     rpn
wait    2
send    12\r
wait    1
send    34\r
wait    1
send    +\r
wait    2
snap
send    q\r
wait    2

shot    checkfile
cap     A cheque-book: a full-screen account manager whose records carry
cap     a date, a type, a description, an account and an amount.  A adds
cap     records, B prints the balance, R reports, F picks the file, Q
cap     quits.
run     checkfile
wait    6
snap
send    q
wait    3

shot    oleo
cap     GNU Oleo 1.6, a spreadsheet.  It stops on an illegal instruction
cap     before it draws a cell, and the process is aborted; sc is the
cap     spreadsheet that runs.
run     oleo
wait    5

shot    scqref
cap     The quick-reference card for sc, the spreadsheet: a document that
cap     prints itself.  These are its first sixteen lines.
run     scqref | head -n 16
wait    12
